From f35f603d8ff3a5f767f34188e59b501b823de647 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mojyack <mojyack@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 08:23:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vd_lavc: create the hwdevice ourselves for DRM PRIME hwdecs

hwdec_create_dev() creates a device itself only for -copy hwdecs; for a
zero-copy one it requires a device published by the VO, matched on both
image format and AVHWDeviceType.  That rule assumes the hwdevice
describes the rendering device, so sharing the VO's is both possible and
necessary.

It does not hold for AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_V4L2REQUEST, whose device is a
decoder session on a V4L2 stateless video node.  No VO can publish one,
and none needs to: what the decoder produces is ordinary DRM PRIME,
which any dmabuf-capable VO imports by image format alone.
vo_dmabuf_wayland publishes IMGFMT_DRMPRIME with AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_DRM,
so the lookup for V4L2REQUEST misses, "Could not create device" is
logged and playback falls back to software.

Fall back to av_hwdevice_ctx_create() when the hwdec's pixel format is
AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME.  Nothing else changes: an hwdec whose device the
VO does publish - including the existing DRM PRIME ones - is matched and
returned before this point, and vaapi, vdpau and cuda do not produce
DRM PRIME at all.

Tested with h264-v4l2request and hevc-v4l2request on a Tegra X1;
--vo=dmabuf-wayland presents the decoder's exported dma-bufs with no
hwdownload and no software fallback.

Assisted-by: Claude (claude-opus-5)
---
 video/decode/vd_lavc.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
index ae199c6..cd57ea1 100644
--- a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
+++ b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
@@ -495,6 +495,13 @@ static AVBufferRef *hwdec_create_dev(struct mp_filter *vd,
             return av_buffer_ref(hw_ctx->av_device_ref);
     }
 
+    if (hwdec->pix_fmt == AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME) {
+        AVBufferRef *ref = NULL;
+
+        if (av_hwdevice_ctx_create(&ref, hwdec->lavc_device, NULL, NULL, 0) >= 0)
+            return ref;
+    }
+
     return NULL;
 }
 
